    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.55,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.15,
    "rationale": "The 18 h aliquot read 0.0575 at 10x dilution (two replicates: 0.0596 and 0.0554), which scales to 0.575. At 40x it read 0.0143 (two replicates), which scales to 0.57. The undiluted reading was 0.531. The diluted samples therefore scale to only about 7-8% above the undiluted reading, and that gap is within the replicate noise. If the reader were saturating, diluted samples would scale up well above the undiluted value, and I saw no such gap. The 10x and 40x results agree with each other. As a linearity control, the 4 h aliquot read 0.0318 at 10x, which scales to 0.318 against 0.330 undiluted, so the reader is linear there. The plateau at about 0.53 from 5 h onward looks like real stationary phase, not detector compression."
